{
    "background_story": "In the depths of the ocean, where the darkness reigns, Azrael, the guardian angel of the sea, watched over the creatures of the deep. With wings as delicate as a batfish, he glided effortlessly through the currents, his presence a beacon of hope. According to legend, Azrael was tasked with guiding lost souls to the afterlife, but he also had a special affinity for the batfish, with their eerie, bat-like fins. He would often descend to the ocean floor, where the batfish dwelled, to offer solace and protection. The batfish, in turn, would gather around him, their bioluminescent bodies lighting up the darkness, as if to illuminate the path for those who sought guidance. Azrael's presence was a reminder that even in the darkest depths, there was always a guardian watching over the sea and its creatures.",
